I didn't say it wasn't. I look at the effort to handle special rules of 
Sokoban to be added code without a lot of benefit for the rest of the 
dungeon. There are certainly Sokoban solvers out there - quite easy to 
find actually. In some ways though, when you think of problems like 
Sokoban (and how people solve them) it gives you ideas that are 
applicable to the main problem (solving Nethack). For example, there are 
a lot of repetitive patterns in solving Sokoban - like when the spoiler 
says "finish" a boulder. About 90% of the time, the rote pattern of 
moving the boulder to the next pit is the "right answer". However in the 
other 10%, you need to get a monster out of the way or battle instead of 
the rote pattern. A bot that can handle that kind of reasoning will 
handle a number of situations in Nethack as well.

